      "title": "Gland Pharma Q2FY27 results: Net profit rises 58% to ₹290.75 crore",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/gland-pharma-q2fy27-results-net-profit-rises-58-to-290-75-crore-126110601734_1.html",
      "description": "Gland Pharma on Friday posted a 58.29 per cent rise in consolidated net profit to Rs 290.75 crore in the September quarter, driven by strong execution across businesses.\nThe company had reported a net profit of Rs 183.68 crore in the year-ago period.\nThe pharmaceutical company's revenue from operations rose to Rs 1,833.58 crore in the quarter under review from Rs 1,486.87 crore a year ago, the company said in a regulatory filing.\nTotal expenses also rose to Rs 1,471.69 crore in the July-September period from Rs 1,287.12 crore a year earlier, it said.\nThe company launched four molecules -- Sugammadex, Erythromycin, Fluorouracil and Atropine sulfate -- in the US this quarter, it said in a release.\nGland Pharma Executive Chairman Srinivas Sadu said, \"We delivered another quarter of strong growth...driven by strong execution across our businesses. Our CDMO business grew 31 per cent year-on-year, supported by expanding customer engagements, strategic partnerships and a robust opportuni",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-06T14:47:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hindalco Q2 result: Net profit jumps 59% to ₹7,533 cr, revenue rises 39%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/hindalco-q2-result-net-profit-jumps-59-to-7-533-cr-revenue-rises-39-126110601026_1.html",
      "description": "Hindalco Industries Ltd on Friday reported 58.8 per cent rise in consolidated net profit at Rs 7,533 crore for September quarter FY27 driven by a strong performance across its business segments.\nNet profit in the year-ago period was Rs 4,741 crore, the Aditya Birla Group metals flagship company said in a BSE filing.\nIncome during the second quarter rose to Rs 92,651 crore over Rs 66,771 crore in the year-ago period, Hindalco Industries said in a filing to BSE.\nIn a statement, the company said this record performance was underpinned by the strength of Hindalco's integrated business model led by a solid primary upstream business complemented by strong contributions from its downstream business.\nHindalco Industries operates across the entire metals value chain, balancing upstream (raw material extraction and basic metal production) and downstream (value-added fabrication and finished products) activities in its aluminium and copper segments.\nEBITDA for the second quarter stood at Rs",
